NAME
       unshare - run a program in new namespaces

SYNOPSIS
       unshare [-u] [-m] [-p] [-i] [-n] [-U] [-C] [-T] [--] [COMMAND [ARG]...]

DESCRIPTION
       Create new namespaces for the calling process and run COMMAND in
       them. Without COMMAND, run $SHELL (or /bin/sh). Requires root.

OPTIONS
       -u, --uts
           new UTS namespace (host name and domain name)

       -m, --mount
       -p, --pid
       -i, --ipc
       -n, --net
       -U, --user
       -C, --cgroup
       -T, --time
           accepted, but report that the namespace is not supported yet

EXAMPLES
       sudo unshare -u sh
       hostname box

SEE ALSO
       nsenter(1), hostname(1)
